IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cr-dates`
IMPORT `cr-client`

-- Cases for cr-client.l4, from the seat of the retail client. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited
-- text, with the provision beside each group; none was copied from the encoding's output. The people, products and
-- figures are hypothetical. Calendar: 2 November 2026 is a Monday; 25 December 2026 is a Friday.

§ `s 1019A, reg 7.9.64 -- do I have a cooling-off right`

-- A year's life cover, new, issued to a retail client: within s 1019A(1)(a)(i), no reg 7.9.64 exclusion.
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a risk insurance product` TRUE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Six-month car cover renewed on its current terms: reg 7.9.64(1)(g) excludes it.
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a risk insurance product` TRUE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Six-month cover that is new, not a renewal: (g)(ii) fails, so not excluded.
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a risk insurance product` TRUE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A renewal on current terms but for 12 months: (g)(i) "less than 12 months" fails, so not excluded.
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a risk insurance product` TRUE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Interim cover (ICA s 11(2)): reg 7.9.64(1)(d).
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a risk insurance product` TRUE TRUE `under an interim contract of insurance` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Super in a fund that is not a public offer fund: reg 7.9.64(1)(f).
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a superannuation product` TRUE TRUE `as a super product of a fund that is not a public offer fund` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Super in a public offer fund, joined directly: s 1019A(1)(a)(iv).
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a superannuation product` TRUE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Units bought by a distribution reinvestment plan: reg 7.9.64(1)(a).
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a managed investment product` TRUE TRUE `under a distribution reinvestment plan or switching facility` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Units in an illiquid scheme: reg 7.9.64(1)(e).
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a managed investment product` TRUE TRUE `as an interest in a scheme or CCIV sub-fund that was not liquid when issued` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Units in a liquid scheme, first investment.
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a managed investment product` TRUE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a foreign passport fund product` TRUE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `an RSA` TRUE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `an investment life insurance product` TRUE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A wholesale client: s 1019A(1)(a) "as a retail client" fails.
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a risk insurance product` FALSE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Bought from another holder, not issued and not a s 1012C sale: s 1019A(1)(b) fails.
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a managed investment product` TRUE FALSE `in none of the excluded ways` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Shares: not one of the s 1019A(1)(a) classes.
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `another kind of financial product` TRUE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A CCIV security: not in the deposited s 1019A(1)(a) list (fork).
#ASSERT `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` `a security in a CCIV` TRUE TRUE `in none of the excluded ways` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 1019B(2), reg 7.9.64A -- how to notify`

#ASSERT `Is this a way I may notify my return` `a superannuation product` `in writing` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a way I may notify my return` `a managed investment product` `electronically` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- By phone, for insurance, where the insurer permits it: reg 7.9.64A.
#ASSERT `Is this a way I may notify my return` `a risk insurance product` `another way, such as by phone` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- By phone, for insurance, where the insurer does not permit it.
#ASSERT `Is this a way I may notify my return` `a risk insurance product` `another way, such as by phone` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- By phone, for super, even if the fund permits it: reg 7.9.64A covers only risk insurance; s 1019B(2) is closed.
#ASSERT `Is this a way I may notify my return` `a superannuation product` `another way, such as by phone` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 1019B(3), (4) -- the last day of the 14-day period`

-- Issued Monday 2 November 2026, no confirmation: the fifth business day after is Monday 9 November (3, 4, 5, 6, 9);
-- the period runs 10 to 23 November.
#ASSERT `The last day of my cooling-off period` (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY EQUALS `the date` 23 11 2026
-- Confirmation received the same day: the period starts then and ends on 16 November.
#ASSERT `The last day of my cooling-off period` (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY EQUALS `the date` 16 11 2026
-- Confirmation on the fifth business day itself: its time is earlier than the end of that day; 9 + 14 = 23 November.
#ASSERT `The last day of my cooling-off period` (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 9 11 2026) EMPTY EQUALS `the date` 23 11 2026
-- Confirmation the day after the fifth business day: (b) is earlier; still 23 November.
#ASSERT `The last day of my cooling-off period` (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 11 2026) EMPTY EQUALS `the date` 23 11 2026
-- Issued Friday 6 November 2026, a public holiday on Tuesday 10 November: business days 9, 11, 12, 13, 16; last day 30
-- November.
#ASSERT `The last day of my cooling-off period` (`the date` 6 11 2026) FALSE (`the date` 6 11 2026) (LIST (`the date` 10 11 2026)) EQUALS `the date` 30 11 2026
-- The same without the holiday: business days 9 to 13; last day 27 November.
#ASSERT `The last day of my cooling-off period` (`the date` 6 11 2026) FALSE (`the date` 6 11 2026) EMPTY EQUALS `the date` 27 11 2026
-- Issued Thursday 24 December 2026, holidays 25 and 28 December and 1 January: business days 29, 30, 31 December, 4, 5
-- January; last day 19 January 2027.
#ASSERT `The last day of my cooling-off period` (`the date` 24 12 2026) FALSE (`the date` 24 12 2026) (LIST (`the date` 25 12 2026), (`the date` 28 12 2026), (`the date` 1 1 2027)) EQUALS `the date` 19 1 2027
-- The same without any holiday: business days 25, 28, 29, 30, 31 December; last day 14 January 2027.
#ASSERT `The last day of my cooling-off period` (`the date` 24 12 2026) FALSE (`the date` 24 12 2026) EMPTY EQUALS `the date` 14 1 2027

§ `s 1019B(3), (5), regs 7.9.65(1), 7.9.70 -- can I still return it on this day`

-- Issued 2 November 2026, no confirmation: the period runs 10 to 23 November.
-- 9 November: the period has not started (s 1019B(3) "can only be exercised during the period").
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 9 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 10 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The last day, and the day after.
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 23 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 24 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Confirmation on 2 November: 2 November itself is in; 16 November in; 17 November out.
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 16 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 17 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A claim already made under the policy: s 1019B(5)(a), Note (a).
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 5 11 2026) TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- One-week cover ending 8 November: s 1019B(5)(b). On 8 November still in; on 9 November out.
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 8 11 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the date` 8 11 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 9 11 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the date` 8 11 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Travel insurance for a trip within the 14 days: before departure in; after departure out (reg 7.9.65(1)).
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 6 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still return my product on this day` (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) EMPTY (`the date` 6 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `reg 7.9.65(1A) -- scheme interests acquired together`

#ASSERT `Must I return all my scheme interests together` `a managed investment product` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I return all my scheme interests together` `a foreign passport fund product` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I return all my scheme interests together` `a managed investment product` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I return all my scheme interests together` `a superannuation product` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `reg 7.9.66 -- returning super or an RSA`

#ASSERT `Must I nominate a fund to return my super` `a superannuation product` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I nominate a fund to return my super` `an RSA` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I nominate a fund to return my super` `a superannuation product` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I nominate a fund to return my super` `a risk insurance product` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Notified 15 January 2027: nominate by 15 February 2027. Notified 31 January 2027: by 28 February 2027 (February has
-- no 31st). Notified 31 January 2028: by 29 February 2028 (a leap year).
#ASSERT `By when must I nominate a fund for my super` `a superannuation product` TRUE (`the date` 15 1 2027) EQUALS JUST (`the date` 15 2 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I nominate a fund for my super` `an RSA` TRUE (`the date` 31 1 2027) EQUALS JUST (`the date` 28 2 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I nominate a fund for my super` `a superannuation product` TRUE (`the date` 31 1 2028) EQUALS JUST (`the date` 29 2 2028)
#ASSERT `By when must I nominate a fund for my super` `a superannuation product` FALSE (`the date` 15 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Notified 15 January 2027; nomination received on the last day, 15 February: taken to be exercised (reg 7.9.66(3)).
#ASSERT `Has my return of my super taken effect` `a superannuation product` TRUE (`the date` 15 1 2027) TRUE (`the date` 15 2 2027) (`the date` 20 2 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Received 16 February, a day late (reg 7.9.66(4)).
#ASSERT `Has my return of my super taken effect` `a superannuation product` TRUE (`the date` 15 1 2027) TRUE (`the date` 16 2 2027) (`the date` 20 2 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Received 1 February: not yet on 31 January, taken effect on 1 February.
#ASSERT `Has my return of my super taken effect` `a superannuation product` TRUE (`the date` 15 1 2027) TRUE (`the date` 1 2 2027) (`the date` 31 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my return of my super taken effect` `a superannuation product` TRUE (`the date` 15 1 2027) TRUE (`the date` 1 2 2027) (`the date` 1 2 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No nomination yet.
#ASSERT `Has my return of my super taken effect` `an RSA` TRUE (`the date` 15 1 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 10 2 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No preserved or restricted money: (3) does not apply; the notice itself exercises the right.
#ASSERT `Has my return of my super taken effect` `a superannuation product` FALSE (`the date` 15 1 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 15 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has my return of my super taken effect` `a superannuation product` FALSE (`the date` 15 1 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 14 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my return of my super taken effect` `a managed investment product` TRUE (`the date` 15 1 2027) TRUE (`the date` 1 2 2027) (`the date` 1 2 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `May my super go to an eligible rollover fund` `a superannuation product` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May my super go to an eligible rollover fund` `an RSA` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May my super go to an eligible rollover fund` `a managed investment product` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 1019B(1), (8), reg 7.9.67 -- how much I get back`

-- A year's cover, premium $1,460 for 365 days, 30 days passed: (8) allows 1,460 x 30 / 365 = $120 off; least $1,340,
-- most $1,460. With $25 of costs under (7): least $1,315.
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `a risk insurance product` FALSE 1460 1460 1460 0 0 1460 365 30 0 EQUALS 1340
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `a risk insurance product` FALSE 1460 1460 1460 0 25 1460 365 30 0 EQUALS 1315
#ASSERT `The most I can be repaid` `a risk insurance product` FALSE 1460 1460 1460 0 EQUALS 1460
-- Insurance: a distribution figure is ignored (reg 7.9.70(1) does not list risk insurance).
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `a risk insurance product` FALSE 1460 1460 1460 0 0 0 0 0 100 EQUALS 1460
-- Units: paid $10,000, worth $9,500 on the notice day: (2) may take off $500; with $50 costs, least $9,450, most $10,000.
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `a managed investment product` FALSE 10000 10000 9500 0 50 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 9450
#ASSERT `The most I can be repaid` `a managed investment product` FALSE 10000 10000 9500 0 EQUALS 10000
-- Worth $10,400: (3) adds $400; least $10,350 (costs), most $10,400.
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `a managed investment product` FALSE 10000 10000 10400 0 50 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 10350
#ASSERT `The most I can be repaid` `a managed investment product` FALSE 10000 10000 10400 0 EQUALS 10400
-- A $300 distribution received: (9) allows it off.
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `a managed investment product` FALSE 10000 10000 10000 0 0 0 0 0 300 EQUALS 9700
-- Super: $5,000 in, worth $5,100, $30 unrecoverable duty: most 5,000 + 100 - 30 = $5,070; less $20 costs: least $5,050.
#ASSERT `The most I can be repaid` `a superannuation product` FALSE 5000 5000 5100 30 EQUALS 5070
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `a superannuation product` FALSE 5000 5000 5100 30 20 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 5050
-- An RSA: no price adjustment (not in (2), (3)) and no costs ((7) excludes RSAs); only tax (6).
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `an RSA` FALSE 2000 2000 1900 0 40 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `an RSA` FALSE 2000 2000 1900 10 40 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 1990
-- Investment life insurance: only an investment-linked product is adjusted.
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `an investment life insurance product` FALSE 1000 1000 900 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `an investment life insurance product` TRUE 1000 1000 900 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 900
-- Reductions larger than the money paid: not below zero (fork).
#ASSERT `The least I can be repaid` `a managed investment product` FALSE 100 100 20 0 50 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 912A(1)(g), reg 7.6.02(5), (6) -- complaints system and AFCA`

#ASSERT `What complaints system must my licensee have` FALSE `in another capacity, such as adviser, insurer, super fund or product issuer` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no dispute resolution system is required by s 912A(1)(g)`
#ASSERT `What complaints system must my licensee have` TRUE `in another capacity, such as adviser, insurer, super fund or product issuer` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `an internal procedure and AFCA membership`
-- A trustee company acting as executor, complaints to a State Ombudsman possible: no AFCA (reg 7.6.02(5)(a)).
#ASSERT `What complaints system must my licensee have` TRUE `as a trustee under a will or on an intestacy` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `an internal procedure, but AFCA membership is not required`
#ASSERT `What complaints system must my licensee have` TRUE `as a trustee under a will or on an intestacy` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an internal procedure and AFCA membership`
#ASSERT `What complaints system must my licensee have` TRUE `as a trustee of an express trust` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `an internal procedure, but AFCA membership is not required`
-- An express trust whose settlor was a company: (5)(b)(i) fails.
#ASSERT `What complaints system must my licensee have` TRUE `as a trustee of an express trust` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `an internal procedure and AFCA membership`
#ASSERT `What complaints system must my licensee have` TRUE `as an attorney under an enduring power of attorney` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `an internal procedure, but AFCA membership is not required`
-- An administrator of an individual's estate under guardianship law: no s 912A(1)(g) system at all (reg 7.6.02(6)).
#ASSERT `What complaints system must my licensee have` TRUE `as the administrator of an individual's estate` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no dispute resolution system is required by s 912A(1)(g)`
-- The same administrator where only an Ombudsman is available: (6) needs a Schedule 8AC law, and (5) does not name
-- administrators.
#ASSERT `What complaints system must my licensee have` TRUE `as the administrator of an individual's estate` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `an internal procedure and AFCA membership`

§ `s 912B, reg 7.6.02AAA -- professional indemnity insurance`

#ASSERT `Must my licensee hold PI insurance to compensate me` TRUE `another licensee, such as an advice business` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my licensee hold PI insurance to compensate me` FALSE `another licensee, such as an advice business` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my licensee hold PI insurance to compensate me` TRUE `an APRA-regulated general insurer` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my licensee hold PI insurance to compensate me` TRUE `an APRA-regulated life insurer` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my licensee hold PI insurance to compensate me` TRUE `an APRA-regulated bank or other ADI` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my licensee hold PI insurance to compensate me` TRUE `a licensee related to an insurer or ADI` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my licensee hold PI insurance to compensate me` TRUE `a licensee related to an insurer or ADI` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my licensee hold PI insurance to compensate me` TRUE `another licensee, such as an advice business` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `reg 7.6.02AA(4) -- the security bond`

#ASSERT `By when must I claim against the security bond` (`the date` 15 3 2027) EQUALS `the date` 15 6 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I claim against the security bond` (`the date` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `the date` 28 2 2027
-- Advertised 15 March 2027, no claim: release possible from 16 June, not on 15 June.
#ASSERT `May ASIC release the security bond` TRUE TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 16 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May ASIC release the security bond` TRUE TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 15 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A valid claim on the last day blocks release; one a day later does not.
#ASSERT `May ASIC release the security bond` TRUE TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2027) TRUE (`the date` 15 6 2027) (`the date` 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May ASIC release the security bond` TRUE TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2027) TRUE (`the date` 16 6 2027) (`the date` 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May ASIC release the security bond` FALSE TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May ASIC release the security bond` TRUE FALSE (`the date` 15 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `regs 7.5.64, 7.5.67-7.5.69 -- a claim on the National Guarantee Fund`

-- Shares and cash held by an ASX broker for a retail client; the broker becomes insolvent owing them.
#ASSERT `Can I claim on the NGF for property my insolvent broker held` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The broker is not insolvent: reg 7.5.64(1)(a) fails.
#ASSERT `Can I claim on the NGF for property my insolvent broker held` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Its obligations had been met before the insolvency: (1)(c) fails.
#ASSERT `Can I claim on the NGF for property my insolvent broker held` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The claimant is the broker's spouse (an excluded person, reg 7.5.04).
#ASSERT `Can I claim on the NGF for property my insolvent broker held` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A loan to the broker: reg 7.5.67.
#ASSERT `Can I claim on the NGF for property my insolvent broker held` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a participant of an SEGC-member market or ACH: reg 7.5.68(a).
#ASSERT `Can I claim on the NGF for property my insolvent broker held` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No securities business in Australia: reg 7.5.68(b).
#ASSERT `Can I claim on the NGF for property my insolvent broker held` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Property already out of the broker's sole control in administering a trust: reg 7.5.69(a).
#ASSERT `Can I claim on the NGF for property my insolvent broker held` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The SEGC is satisfied the claimant materially contributed to the insolvency: reg 7.5.69(b).
#ASSERT `Can I claim on the NGF for property my insolvent broker held` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `reg 7.5.70 -- by when, and is a late claim barred`

-- A Form 720 notice naming 30 September 2027: that day.
#ASSERT `By when must I make my NGF claim` TRUE (`the date` 30 9 2027) (`the date` 15 3 2027) EQUALS `the date` 30 9 2027
-- No notice; aware on 15 March 2027: six months, 15 September 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I make my NGF claim` FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 15 3 2027) EQUALS `the date` 15 9 2027
-- No notice; aware on 31 August 2027: 29 February 2028 (no 31 February; 2028 is a leap year).
#ASSERT `By when must I make my NGF claim` FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `the date` 29 2 2028
-- Served on the last day: not barred. A day later: barred (reg 7.5.70(3)), unless the SEGC determines otherwise.
#ASSERT `Is my NGF claim barred` FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 15 3 2027) (`the date` 15 9 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my NGF claim barred` FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 15 3 2027) (`the date` 16 9 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my NGF claim barred` FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 15 3 2027) (`the date` 16 9 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- With a notice naming 30 September 2027, a claim served on 1 October is barred, though within six months of awareness.
#ASSERT `Is my NGF claim barred` TRUE (`the date` 30 9 2027) (`the date` 15 6 2027) (`the date` 1 10 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `reg 7.5.72B(1) -- the claimant limit`

-- $300,000 of cash: limited to $250,000.
#ASSERT `The most the NGF may pay me` 300000 0 EQUALS 250000
-- $100,000 cash and $500,000 of shares: $600,000, under both limits.
#ASSERT `The most the NGF may pay me` 100000 500000 EQUALS 600000
-- Exactly at both limits: $250,000 cash and $750,000 shares: $1,000,000.
#ASSERT `The most the NGF may pay me` 250000 750000 EQUALS 1000000
-- $300,000 cash and $900,000 shares: 250,000 + 900,000 = 1,150,000, limited to $1,000,000.
#ASSERT `The most the NGF may pay me` 300000 900000 EQUALS 1000000
-- One dollar over the $1 million limit in shares alone.
#ASSERT `The most the NGF may pay me` 0 1000001 EQUALS 1000000

§ `regs 7.5.78, 7.5.79 -- costs and interest`

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to my NGF claim costs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to my NGF claim costs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to my NGF claim costs` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- $100,000 from 1 January to 15 March 2027 (73 days) at 5%: 100,000 x 0.05 x 73 / 365 = $1,000.
#ASSERT `The interest the NGF must pay me` 100000 (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 15 3 2027) 0 EQUALS 1000
-- At a determined 7%: $1,400.
#ASSERT `The interest the NGF must pay me` 100000 (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 15 3 2027) 0.07 EQUALS 1400
-- A "determined" 4% is below the reg 7.5.79(2)(b) floor: 5% applies, $1,000.
#ASSERT `The interest the NGF must pay me` 100000 (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 15 3 2027) 0.04 EQUALS 1000
-- A full year, 1 January 2027 to 1 January 2028 (365 days): $5,000.
#ASSERT `The interest the NGF must pay me` 100000 (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 1 1 2028) 0 EQUALS 5000

§ `reg 7.9.66 -- the nomination as a regulative rule`

-- Notified on day 0, 31 days allowed: a nomination on day 31 fulfils the duty; the return then waits on the responsible
-- person returning the money as directed.
#TRACE `the return of my super` 31 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the holder` DOES `nominate a superannuation entity or RSA` AT 31
    PARTY `the responsible person` DOES `return the money as directed` AT 40
